WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.703
The revolt of 1857 was crushed.

2
00:00:02.903 --> 00:00:04.494
Yet it ended the East India

3
00:00:04.494 --> 00:00:05.378
Company's rule.

4
00:00:05.878 --> 00:00:08.559
On 10 May 1857, sepoys at

5
00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:09.846
Meerut rose,

6
00:00:09.946 --> 00:00:11.269
and marched to Delhi.

7
00:00:11.669 --> 00:00:13.225
Rebels proclaimed Bahadur

8
00:00:13.225 --> 00:00:14.906
Shah Zafar, the last Mughal

9
00:00:14.906 --> 00:00:16.213
ruler, their emperor.

10
00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:18.402
The trigger: new cartridges,

11
00:00:18.402 --> 00:00:20.078
reportedly greased with cow

12
00:00:20.078 --> 00:00:20.823
and pig fat.

13
00:00:20.973 --> 00:00:22.795
Behind it: annexations, and

14
00:00:22.795 --> 00:00:23.874
long grievances.

15
00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.497
Why did it fail?

16
00:00:25.747 --> 00:00:27.278
It stayed mostly in the north

17
00:00:27.278 --> 00:00:27.859
and centre,

18
00:00:27.959 --> 00:00:29.709
with no single plan or leader,

19
00:00:29.809 --> 00:00:31.342
and many rulers sided with

20
00:00:31.342 --> 00:00:33.051
a better-armed British force.

21
00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:35.578
In 1858, an Act of Parliament

22
00:00:35.578 --> 00:00:37.584
moved power from the Company

23
00:00:37.584 --> 00:00:38.515
to the Crown.

24
00:00:38.965 --> 00:00:40.245
A lost revolt.

25
00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:41.767
A changed Raj.

26
00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:43.163
Your turn.

27
00:00:43.463 --> 00:00:45.362
What did the Government of

28
00:00:45.362 --> 00:00:46.749
India Act, 1858 do?
